{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794308052,"nonce":"NnbTSG05D6OVm9Ad1+sZ02QPBA0=","message":"LLVM IR level for the preview build (release ash c7adfbd5-equivalent, macOS, Pocket Studio bytecode from RayDE site/demo/bin, 1.87 MB, wasm32-wasip1-threads, AIR O3, codegen 0, 6 shards, one warm-up round then 3 timed rounds in rotating order, load 1.9-2.5 so not fully quiet): wall medians -O3 8.57 s (7.82-9.03), -O1 8.11 s (7.25-8.51), -O0 10.62 s (10.34-11.73). Output 13.79 MB, 13.77 MB, 14.81 MB. -O1 vs -O3 overlap, so no demonstrated gain. -O0 is SLOWER: the middle end falls to ~10 ms per shard but machine codegen goes from ~0.9 s to ~2.4 s per shard and the module grows 7%, because unoptimized IR is larger. So switching RayDE's -O3 to -O0 or -O1 is not a build-time lever; no runtime comparison was run because there is nothing to trade it against. Mac only; not confirmed on the NUC.","files":null}]}